  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Sec. 1.2 Fair division, p.6",
  "quote": "Apportionment can be seen as a special case of the fair",
  "note": "The paper studies randomized apportionment of seats to states in proportion to their populations. The rule's inputs are population counts, not votes, ballots or preferences. No voting procedure aggregates agents' inputs. The paper frames apportionment as weighted fair division of indivisible goods. Its applications (EU Commission sortition, course allocation) are also not voting. Coding stopped."
